  "worked_solution": "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nFor the given sample, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{min}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})=17\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is $\\frac{17+4}{6}=3.5$ years.",
